WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.598
Steps seven and eight read
the same secret twice,

2
00:00:03.598 --> 00:00:06.525
on the test V M, so the
network allows both.

3
00:00:06.525 --> 00:00:10.421
First as the V M's managed
identity, which has the Key Vault

4
00:00:10.421 --> 00:00:14.400
Secrets User role on the vault:
the secret's name comes back.

5
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.898
Then as yourself, with no
data-plane role on the vault:

6
00:00:17.898 --> 00:00:20.338
the request is refused as forbidden.

7
00:00:20.338 --> 00:00:23.424
The network allowed it;
role-based access didn't.

8
00:00:23.424 --> 00:00:26.450
That's the pair the guide's
Validate step asks for.

9
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:31.025
Step nine, back on your machine,
finds both reads in the audit log.

10
00:00:31.025 --> 00:00:36.165
The guide's diagnostic setting writes to
the workspace's Azure Diagnostics table,

11
00:00:36.165 --> 00:00:40.700
and Learn's page, Monitor Azure Key
Vault, filters it by resource provider.

12
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:46.713
Its result signature column holds the H
T T P status, such as O K or Forbidden.

13
00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.737
Expect a row for each read.

14
00:00:48.737 --> 00:00:52.809
Step ten: both az logout commands
signed you out of the test V M,

15
00:00:52.809 --> 00:00:56.540
and nothing in Azure changed,
so there's nothing to undo.
